  "why": "The Exiled Heavy Knight Knows How to Game the System is a 26 episode run airing 2026-07-03 to 2026-12-25 across two cours, eleven episodes out by the time of labelling. anilist:180136, kitsu:49183, mal:59741 and offline:mal-59741 are one run: anilist gives mal:59741, kitsu and offline give anilist:180136, and anilist, kitsu and mal all carry the 2026-07-03 start with 26 episodes. anizip:18854 is the same run: it maps to mal:59741 and anilist:180136 and lists 26 episodes on the run's weekly Thursday schedule from 2026-07-02. The Crunchyroll season cr:GT00378018-GS00378019 is the same run, not a container: anilist itself gives it as SAME_AS, its 11 episodes fall on 2026-07-02 to 2026-09-10, the same days anizip gives episodes 1 to 11, and its count of 11 is short of the run's 26 rather than over it. The JustWatch season jw:454469-474794 is the same run as well: all 11 of its episode titles, from I'm Elymas the Heavy Knight to Inescapable Past, are the exact non-generic titles Crunchyroll gives the same 11 positions. cr:GT00378018 is a bare Crunchyroll series id with no season, dates or count, so it holds the run. Episodes pair anizip to Crunchyroll on matching release days for episodes 1 to 11 (episode 1's titles differ slightly, Elymas the Heavy Knight against I'm Elymas the Heavy Knight, but both sit on 2026-07-02), and JustWatch to Crunchyroll on the 11 exact titles; the kitsu episode rows carry no title or date and place nothing. The Netflix season nf:82942166-1 lists 11 episodes titled Episode 1 to Episode 11 with no dates against a 26 episode run, so it is left unsettled."
